&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every day, you move. Cycling, typing on a keyboard, playing an instrument &amp;ndash; all of it is controlled by a  finely-tuned process that your brain, nerves, and muscles follow in order to translate your intentions into accurate, fine movements. This multi-system process doesn&amp;rsquo;t always go perfectly, however: Maybe you have experienced shaky hands or legs after a workout, or an annoying bout of hiccups.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
